## Install commands for all 15

The hosted zip is the quick path and works everywhere. The `degit` path pulls the whole skill folder from GitHub, including scripts and reference files. On November 25, 2026 we ran both: we downloaded all 15 hosted zips and unzipped them (each contained one file, SKILL.md), and we ran `npx degit` for all 15 source folders, which all exited with code 0 and produced the file counts below.

| Skill | Hosted zip (id) | Files via degit |
|---|---|---|
| Webapp Testing | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/47 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/webapp-testing` | 6 |
| Git Commit | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/546 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/git-commit` | 1 |
| Resolve Conflicts | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/2048 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts` | 5 |
| Code Reviewer | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/527 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/code-reviewer` | 1 |
| Code Review Excellence | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/741 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/code-review-excellence` | 3 |
| Debugging Strategies | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/2609 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/debugging-strategies` | 2 |
| Python Testing Patterns | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/138 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/python-testing-patterns` | 3 |
| Vitest | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/1479 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/vitest` | 21 |
| Refactor | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/515 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/refactor` | 1 |
| Git Advanced Workflows | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/84 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/git-advanced-workflows` | 2 |
| Dependency Upgrade | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/351 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/dependency-upgrade` | 1 |
| Software Architecture | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/658 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/software-architecture` | 1 |
| Docs Architect | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/2971 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/docs-architect` | 1 |
| Claude Automation Recommender | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/848 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/claude-automation-recommender` | 6 |
| Subagent Driven Development | `curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/502 -o skill.zip && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/subagent-driven-development` | 4 |

The `degit` form for each is `npx degit <owner>/<repo>/<path> ~/.claude/skills/<slug>`, and the source path is on each skill's catalog page and in its section above. For a project-level install, replace `~/.claude/skills/` with `.claude/skills/` and commit the folder.

{% callout type="warning" %}
For nine of the 15 skills (Webapp Testing, Resolve Conflicts, Code Review Excellence, Debugging Strategies, Python Testing Patterns, Vitest, Git Advanced Workflows, Claude Automation Recommender, Subagent Driven Development), the hosted zip contains only SKILL.md while the GitHub folder has more. Several of those SKILL.md files tell the agent to read a reference file or run a script that the zip does not include. Use `degit` for those nine, or copy the folder from GitHub.
{% /callout %}

Two small gotchas we hit while reading. Resolve Conflicts hardcodes `.forge/skills/resolve-conflicts/scripts/` paths, which do not exist in a `~/.claude/skills/` install, so adjust them. Code Reviewer hardcodes `npm run preflight`, so tell the agent to use your own test command.

## Works-with matrix

Skills are an open format, and each of these clients documents a folder-with-SKILL.md layout. We read each client's skills documentation on November 25, 2026 and list the directories it documents. "Yes" below means the client documents loading a skill folder from that path. It does not mean we ran the skill in that client, because we did not.

| Client | Documented skill paths | Loads these 15 skills? | Caveats from the skills themselves |
|---|---|---|---|
| Claude Code | `~/.claude/skills/`, `.claude/skills/` | Yes | Subagent Driven Development and Claude Automation Recommender are written for Claude Code concepts |
| Codex | `$HOME/.agents/skills`, `$REPO_ROOT/.agents/skills`, `/etc/codex/skills` | Yes (format) | Install to `.agents/skills`; the subagent skill assumes TodoWrite |
| Cursor | `.cursor/skills/`, `.agents/skills/`, plus compatibility loading of `.claude/skills/` and `.codex/skills/` | Yes (format) | The recommender's output is framed around Claude Code hooks, subagents and plugins |
| Gemini CLI | `~/.gemini/skills/`, `.gemini/skills/`, and the `.agents/skills/` alias | Yes (format) | Code Reviewer and Docs Changelog originate in the Gemini CLI repo |
| OpenCode | `.opencode/skills/`, `~/.config/opencode/skills`, compatibility `.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills` | Yes (format) | None specific |
| Hermes | `~/.hermes/skills/` | Yes (format) | None specific |

"Format" means the SKILL.md layout is the documented standard for that client; the skills in this list are plain instructions plus optional scripts, so they should work, but a skill that says "dispatch a subagent" needs the client to have subagents. Practical shortcut: Cursor and OpenCode both document loading `.claude/skills`, and Gemini CLI, Cursor, OpenCode and Codex all document `.agents/skills`, so one install in `.agents/skills/` covers four of the six clients.

